      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the total dose is too high.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg per day**. The highest recommended daily dose of metformin is:\n- **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release (usually 850 mg three times daily)\n- **2000 mg/day** for extended-release\n\nSo this order is about twice the maximum. It looks like it could be a transcription error. Two common orders that fit the numbers:\n- **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n- **Metformin 1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n\nCan you confirm which dose you meant? If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a reason. I'll add it as a note on the order so pharmacy can see it.\n\nAlso, is this the patient's home dose or a new start? If it's a new start, it's usually best to begin low (for example, 500 mg once or twice daily) and increase gradually to limit stomach side effects."
      }
     ],
